{"id": "EUVD-2026-81927", "enisaUuid": "b3d1ef31-e096-356d-860a-e745abd9b044", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsamples/ftrace: Fix kthread_stop() on ERR_PTR in ftrace-direct-multi-modify\n\nftrace_direct_multi_init() assigns kthread_run()'s return value to\nsimple_tsk without an IS_ERR() check. When kthread_run() fails it\nreturns ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM), but init still returns 0, so the module loads\nwith simple_tsk holding an error pointer. On unload,\nftrace_direct_multi_exit() then passes that ERR_PTR to kthread_stop(),\nleading to a null-pointer-dereference.\n\nCheck the return value of kthread_run() with IS_ERR(); on failure,\nunregister the ftrace direct call and propagate the error code.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:05:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a96b9f6d5ba23dbce66c8a4a242effd4c01a830", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/98b7b2a29ae87937aa02ab9391543ef8c602cd94", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/626614df9080d7052fbe24dc90b5434717ab7a9f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf839636911d8313f3ecd098329fd0b96499e4cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6727b7618f49401acf373fa3ec5712e2ec52e5cf"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90066", "GHSA-h42m-cfhq-9g8c"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14251c91-ff90-37c8-ac00-08254a681794", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1067a07cfbc5a36abad3752fafe4c79e06db1bb <98b7b2a29ae87937aa02ab9391543ef8c602cd94"}, {"id": "19f2c535-905a-3f4b-b7d2-2580fb738fb4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1b08f9fb-717c-3221-a202-510347ce5616", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "2ad7dc6d-8b78-3d03-ab0d-c32989e2b834", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5f0cd604-626f-32fc-b302-b5a01b908de4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "6446a6cd-c371-3e05-bd13-ecc4c10c782d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "6e57432c-5992-3d4a-8381-d01bac7a85c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1067a07cfbc5a36abad3752fafe4c79e06db1bb <6727b7618f49401acf373fa3ec5712e2ec52e5cf"}, {"id": "7ffce829-c3df-3e68-a0ec-5c61918310a0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1067a07cfbc5a36abad3752fafe4c79e06db1bb <cf839636911d8313f3ecd098329fd0b96499e4cf"}, {"id": "e48e7957-b7c9-34f6-ba42-87aac31837e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1067a07cfbc5a36abad3752fafe4c79e06db1bb <7a96b9f6d5ba23dbce66c8a4a242effd4c01a830"}, {"id": "e546efff-5d98-3a1a-88f6-66945c727c63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "e768273e-dfc1-3a49-bc4c-4cc20235fc0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1067a07cfbc5a36abad3752fafe4c79e06db1bb <626614df9080d7052fbe24dc90b5434717ab7a9f"}, {"id": "f1602405-e903-3050-9023-22819e3aea63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3afa71a5-ec6f-3869-b44a-c8a651d9162b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}